0. HOW TO FILL SOURCE FILES IF PHOTO HAS WEIRD ANGLE
- cut the photo to most correct shape
- find corners where notebook curves
- take closest to curve paper colour (pipet)
- make new layer, put colour on corners to mimic paper
- add Gauss distortion (19' is checked value)
- try playing with layer transparency to match
- with harder materials:
  - select rectangle of more-less clean material
  - use "soften selection" tool, 50' is checked value
  - try to copy-paste it near requested space, making transition

I. SEITEH NAME ETYMOLOGY
= ehr. ct'eh - whole world          | ct' + eh
= ghl. sh'sta'h - origin of all     | sh' + sta'h

Ct' >> (sst)
Eh  >> (eh)

= ehr. "ssteh"
= ghl. "shhstaah"
= ghl. "sejitaah" (IV era) <seyta'h>
= bae. "seiteh" (ehr./ghl.)

II. TARSKIGG & NORDWINIAN LANGUAGE
Tarskigg = tar + skigg

> Tar - elders
> Skigg - meeting, gathering

Plural is default of some words, such as 'tar', resembling
tribalic mindset

-od is suffix used to signify "I do something"

For example:
             Kalahod (kalahod)

"I do the ritual"

Kalah - to do ritual (kala:, "...h" is silent)
-od   - signify first-person actor

Kalahagad - wrath of gods, usually due to sacrilege (kalahaga:d)
Agad - wrath (aga:d)
Lig - strong (Heim-lig baedoorian name suffix)

