IV. ENCHANTED ITEMS
Enchanting items is difficult, as it requires scroll-like unbounding,
so wearer/user should be both good at dodging-and-magic, fighting-and-magic,
so it's really obscure choice and rather unliked by requirements it sets.
Additionally, it requires really good timing, as it needs unbounding at
the second of hitting the enemy.
Enchanting gear is actually easier than using said gear.

This is why rods are used to TRANSFER energy into spell, not as something
adjecent to the rod itself - hitting someone with rod is extremely weak
and would be tough to work with. Transfering, in the other hand, means
that you have three steps:

       CAST SPELL TO YOU ---> CAST INTO ROD
                                  ---> UNBOUND AND CAST INTO TARGET

It may come in handy, to some extent, though it lenghtens the process
a lot

It also explains why mages wear enchanted robes instead of armour - it is
easier to unbound enchant from such light material than it is from more
solid thing

V. GHLODDISH REQUESTED WORDS:
- end / ending (as there is 'beginning')
- :ar': for several god-like aspects (to be, letter, sentence, mirror - all of
  them have metaphysical qualities connected to christian The Word, which is
  understood specifically in Baedoor oververse concept, y'remember)